    {
      "id": "HI-C69-vehicle",
      "sequence": 2880,
      "title": "गाड़ी (gāṛī) — a vehicle; a train",
      "headword": "गाड़ी",
      "romanization": "gāṛī",
      "gloss": "a vehicle; a train",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:e6d94b18c6547fbe",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words back before anything new: what does bhāshā mean, and what is अंग्रेज़ी? The next five words are how you leave the शहर you live in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: गाड़ी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गाड़ी (gāṛī) — \"a vehicle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit गर्त (garta), a cart, through the Prakrits. It began as the thing oxen pulled and it has taken in everything since: a car is a गाड़ी (gāṛī), a train is a गाड़ी (gāṛī), a bullock cart is a गाड़ी (gāṛī)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That width is the reason to learn it first. बस you already own, and बस names one thing only. गाड़ी (gāṛī) names whatever is carrying you, so it is the word that never leaves you stuck — point at anything with wheels and गाड़ी (gāṛī) is right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ड़ in the middle is the flapped retroflex, made by flicking the tongue down off the roof of the mouth. It is ड with the nuqta underneath."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five words for getting somewhere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say bhāshā, then read अंग्रेज़ी and say what it means",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *bhāshā*, then read **अंग्रेज़ी** and say what it means]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "gāṛī, slowly, with the flap in the middle",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *gāṛī*, slowly, with the flap in the middle]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gāṛī",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gāṛī*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "CONTRAST",
              "instruction": "gāṛī and bas, and say which one is wider",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU CONTRAST: *gāṛī* and *bas*, and say which one is wider]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does गाड़ी (gāṛī) mean? (\"a vehicle\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HI-C69-railway",
      "sequence": 2890,
      "title": "रेल (rel) — the railway",
      "headword": "रेल",
      "romanization": "rel",
      "gloss": "the railway",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:9f5b7a9604c3f795",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say gāṛī, then write गाड़ी: ग, then the ा stroke, then ड with its nuqta, then ी. Four pieces, all of them yours already."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: रेल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रेल (rel) — \"the railway\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English rail, borrowed whole in the nineteenth century and spelt with the े matra, which is where an English ay sound usually lands in Devanagari."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रेल (rel) on its own is the system: the network, the line, the railway as an institution. The train itself is रेलगाड़ी — रेल (rel) plus the गाड़ी (gāṛī) you learnt in the last lesson — and in speech people shorten that back to plain गाड़ी (gāṛī). Two words you now hold combine into the third without anything new."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गाड़ी (gāṛī) and रेल (rel), and the compound they make between them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "read अंग्रेज़ी, then say it without looking",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: read **अंग्रेज़ी**, then say it without looking]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
