    {
      "id": "HI-C69-station",
      "sequence": 2900,
      "title": "स्टेशन (sṭeshan) — a station",
      "headword": "स्टेशन",
      "romanization": "sṭeshan",
      "gloss": "a station",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:9cd0607abb0af225",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which of your two words names the network, and which names the thing that moves along it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: स्टेशन",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "स्टेशन (sṭeshan) — \"a station\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English station, and it shows its seams. Hindi does not open a word with two consonants stuck together, so the writing does it the Devanagari way instead: स with the vowel-killer ् underneath, then ट. That stack is the same virama you met inside नमस्ते."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The retroflex ट rather than dental त is deliberate. When Hindi borrows an English t, it hears the English tongue as curled back, so station becomes स्टेशन (sṭeshan) and not स्तेशन. Every English t you meet in a Hindi loan will do this."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is painted on every platform board in the country, in Devanagari and in Latin letters side by side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: गाड़ी (gāṛī), रेल (rel), स्टेशन (sṭeshan). A vehicle, a network, and the place you wait."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "READ",
              "instruction": "स्टेशन (sṭeshan), and find the ् that stacks the first two letters",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU READ: स्टेशन, and find the ् that stacks the first two letters]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "sṭeshan",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *sṭeshan*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
